    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0358" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v02/pg327"/>

                <head>158. Memorandum by the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d158-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1971-07-20">July 20, 1971</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="description">
                    <label>MEMORANDUM FOR</label>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>The Director of Central Intelligence</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has directed that Departments and Agencies concerned refrain from
                    commenting on the implications of his July 15, 1971 announcement concerning the
                    People’s Republic of China.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d158-f2"/> This directive
                    applies to both on the record and background statements as <pb facs="0359"
                        n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> well as to inquiries within official and diplomatic
                    channels. In those instances where it is considered that substantive statements
                    must be made, he has asked that such statements be cleared with him through the
                    office of the Assistant to the President for National Security Affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Henry A. Kissinger<anchor n="3" xml:id="d158-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d158-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d158-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Security Council, Secretariat, Directives, 1971, Directive #89.
                    Confidential. A copy was sent to Moorer.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d158-f2" n="2" xml:id="d158-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the President’s remarks to the nation announcing acceptance of an
                    invitation to visit the People’s Republic of China, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Public Papers: Nixon, 1971</hi>, pp. 819–820. Nixon visited the People’s
                    Public of China February 21–28, 1972.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d158-f3" n="3" xml:id="d158-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
